==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From Germanic ''*mēnōþ-'', from Indo-European ''*mēnōt-'' ‘month, moon’.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''mōnath'', Old Saxon ''mānuð'' (Dutch [[maand]]), Old High German ''mānōd'' (German [[Monat]]), Old Norse ''mānaðr'' (Danish {{term|Måned}} Swedish [[månad]]), Gothic [[𐌼𐌴𐌽𐍉𐌸𐍃]] (menoþs).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/'mo:naθ/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
'''mōnaþ''' ''m'' (''pl'' '''mōnaþas''' or '''mōnaþ''')

# [[month]]

===Etymology 2===
See [[manian]].

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/'monaθ/|lang=ang}}

====Verb form====
'''monaþ'''

# variant spelling of the third-person singular present of [[manian]]

